{{/*
  phase-guidelines-footer — the trailing three bullets that close the
  `## Guidelines` block of every beads-issues **phase** prompt. These
  bullets are near-identical across all 7 phases with only three
  degrees of freedom:

    * whether the "Live state only" bullet mentions `Item.*` (only the
      plan + investigate phases still do, because they run first in
      their respective driver and callers historically leaned on the
      last-run `Item.*` payload — dropped for the phases that always
      re-enter after a Commit step).
    * the tier-comment noun (\"plan\" for plan, \"findings\" for
      investigate, \"summary\" for the rest) that the operator's
      `bd comment` should carry.
    * the tier-comment prefix word (\"Plan\", \"Implementation\",
      \"Testing\", \"Review\", \"Reproduction\", \"Investigation\",
      \"Fix\") + declared .Tier (\"Reasoning\" / \"Coding\").

  Consumers: feature-phase-plan / -implement / -test / -review,
  fix-phase-reproduce / -investigate / -fix.

  Usage:

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/phase-guidelines-footer" (dict
          "IncludeItemNote" true
          "TagNoun"         "plan"
          "TagPrefix"       "Plan"
          "Tier"            "Reasoning"
      ) }}

  Parameters:
    IncludeItemNote — bool; when true, appends " or from `Item.*`"
                      to the Live-state bullet. Used by the plan +
                      investigate phases; false for all others.
    TagNoun         — the noun after "Prefix the " (e.g., "plan",
                      "summary", "findings").
    TagPrefix       — the leading word of the tier-tagged bd comment
                      (e.g., "Plan", "Implementation", "Testing",
                      "Review", "Reproduction", "Investigation",
                      "Fix").
    Tier            — "Reasoning" or "Coding"; declared model tier
                      for the phase.

  Uses only builtin text/template actions so it is safe to attach to
  every render context, including the narrow-FuncMap target.title path.
*/}}
- **Live state only.** Always re-read labels via `bd show --json` at the start of
  the phase; never assume labels from a prior run{{ if .IncludeItemNote }} or from `Item.*`{{ end }}.
- **Always log to the tracker** with `bd comment` so progress is auditable.
- **Tier tag every comment.** Prefix the {{ .TagNoun }} with `{{ .TagPrefix }} [tier: {{ .Tier }}]:` so
  the tier split is observable in the bead history (mitto-mpu5 acceptance criteria).
